# 39. COMMON MISTAKES

### Mistake 1

Only checking for:

```text
..
```

❌ Not sufficient.

### Mistake 2

Using client-side validation.

❌ Client-side controls can be bypassed.

### Mistake 3

Assuming URL encoding automatically makes traversal safe.

❌ Encoding and decoding behavior must be understood.

### Mistake 4

Allowing users to specify arbitrary filesystem paths.

❌ Prefer application-controlled file IDs.

### Mistake 5

Running the application with excessive filesystem permissions.

❌ Follow least privilege.

