# 🎯 ONE-LINE EXAM ANSWER

> **Directory Traversal is a vulnerability in which improperly handled user-controlled path information allows an application to access files or directories outside its intended location; it is mitigated by using controlled file identifiers, canonicalizing and validating resolved paths, safe archive extraction, allowlists, and least-privilege filesystem permissions.**